643	766	614	614	I	0	’ War , and the vaulted chapel , with its brick floor worn by pious peasant knees , is now used as a hall . Gustavus Adolphus and his Swedes passed through more than once , as is duly recorded in archives still preserved , for we are on what was then the high - road between Sweden and Brandenburg the unfortunate . The Lion of the North was no doubt an estimable person and acted wholly up to his convictions , but he must have sadly upset the peaceful nuns , who were not without convictions of their own , sending them out on to the wide , empty plain to piteously seek some life to replace the life of silence here .
